      "entries": [
        "60 feet. A nasurgeth's entropy grows even stronger underwater. All water within the aura is completely dark (as 4th-level darkness). Magical light with a counteract level of 4th level or lower, along with magical light cantrips, are suppressed. A living creature entering or starting its turn in the aura takes 4d6 negative damage, and the creature also takes an additional 2d10 cold damage if it's in water (DC 39 basic Fortitude save). If it fails, it's also enfeebled 1 for 1 minute and pulled 10 feet toward the nasurgeth."
